  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# **Capstone**: EDA for the PM2.5 in NYC, May-2026\n",
        "\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "OmDswAO43PK1"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# **0. Introduction**"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "4mqb-9MsMVz5"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## **Context**\n",
        "PM2.5 refers to fine particulate matter that is 2.5 micrometers or smaller in diameter and is considered one of the most harmful air pollutants because it can travel deep into the lungs and affect heart and respiratory health. In NYC, long-term exposure to PM2.5 is linked to an estimated 2,000 excess deaths from lung and heart disease each year, while short-term exposure can contribute to asthma-related emergency department visits and other health threats; in this project, PM2.5 is measured in µg/m³ to evaluate air quality patterns across monitoring locations. (1).\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "(1) https://a816-dohbesp.nyc.gov/IndicatorPublic/data-features/realtime-air-quality/\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "dNs2p2jP4XHM"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## N**ew York City PM₂.₅ Air Quality Tracking Framework**\n",
        "\n",
        "| Feature | 1‑Hour Framework | 24‑Hour Regulatory Standard | Annual / Baseline Metrics |\n",
        "|---------|------------------|-----------------------------|----------------------------|\n",
        "| **Legal Status** | No statutory limit (no legal penalty or fines apply) | Legally binding federal threshold | — |\n",
        "| **Threshold Value** | N/A (tracks live raw metrics only) | **35 µg/m³** | — |\n",
        "| **Pristine Reference** | — | — | 2.5 µg/m³ (pristine background air; zero health risk) |\n",
        "| **Clinical Threshold** | **10 µg/m³** incremental spike triggers measurable increases in heart/lung hospital visits | — | — |\n",
        "| **Primary Purpose** | Immediate public alerts and short‑term visibility | Federal regulatory compliance and regional state planning | — |\n",
        "| **Data Calculation** | NowCast Algorithm (weights the last 12 hours of rolling data) | Strict midnight‑to‑midnight calendar‑day blocks | — |\n",
        "| **Compliance Test** | N/A | 3‑year average of annual 98th percentile values | — |\n",
        "| **Reporting Tool** | Live AirNow AQI maps and phone alerts | NYSDEC annual regulatory reports | — |\n",
        "| **Framework Inception** | — | — | 2006 (24‑hour limit lowered to 35 µg/m³) |\n",
        "| **AQI Formula Update** | — | — | 2012 (NowCast algorithm standardized for modern maps) |\n",
        "| **Recent Policy Revision** | — | — | 2024 (annual baseline lowered to 9 µg/m³) [1, 2] |\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "The project will therefore use two interpretation levels:\n",
        "1. **Primary threshold**: 24-hour PM2.5 standard of 35 micrograms per cubic meter, evaluated using daily station averages.\n",
        "2. **Secondary clinical spike flag**: short-term PM2.5 spikes that may deserve attention even when the 24-hour standard is not exceeded.\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "ktekDQhaC3GR"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## **Problem Statement**\n",
        "\n",
        "The project investigates PM2.5 air quality patterns in NYC during May 1-19, 2026.\n",
        "\n",
        "The key problem is that overall air quality can appear acceptable while some places and hours may still experience short-term PM2.5 increases. The analysis should identify whether PM2.5 levels remained below relevant thresholds, where the highest peaks occurred, where the lowest levels appeared, and whether short-term spikes deserve attention.\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "n6XN5qfTy0Hv"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## **Project Objective**\n",
        "Analyze hourly PM2.5 measurements from NYC street-level monitors for May 1-19, 2026, using exploratory data analysis to identify overall patterns, missing values, station-level differences, peak values, low values, threshold status, and practical recommendations.\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "sAMKBbovzJhQ"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## **Analysis Questions**\n",
        "\n",
        "1. What is the overall PM2.5 pattern in NYC during May 1-19, 2026?\n",
        "2. Are observed PM2.5 values generally below the 24-hour standard of 35 micrograms per cubic meter?\n",
        "3. Which monitoring locations recorded the highest PM2.5 peaks?\n",
        "4. Which monitoring locations recorded the lowest PM2.5 levels?\n",
        "5. How does PM2.5 vary by time and station location?\n",
        "6. Are there missing values or data-quality issues that affect interpretation?\n",
        "7. Were there short-term PM2.5 spikes that deserve attention even if the 24-hour standard was not exceeded?\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "doWUZuZ5z0CG"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## **Dataset Description**\n",
        "The dataset contains hourly PM2.5 air quality measurements from NYC monitoring stations for May 1–19, 2026, with each record including a site ID, timestamp, and PM2.5 value in µg/m³. A separate station metadata file provides location names and geographic coordinates, allowing the analysis to compare PM2.5 patterns across monitoring locations.\n",
        "\n",
        "### **Main Dataset Fields**:\n",
        "\n",
        "| Field | Meaning |\n",
        "|-------|---------|\n",
        "| **[ID](ca://s?q=Explain_the_ID_field_in_this_dataset)** | Record identifier. |\n",
        "| **[SiteID](ca://s?q=What_is_the_SiteID_field_used_for)** | Monitoring station identifier. |\n",
        "| **[ObservationTimeUTC](ca://s?q=Explain_ObservationTimeUTC_timestamp_format)** | Timestamp for the start of the hourly measurement period. |\n",
        "| **[Value](ca://s?q=What_does_the_PM2.5_Value_field_represent)** | PM₂.₅ concentration in micrograms per cubic meter. |\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "### **Station Metadata Fields**:\n",
        "\n",
        "| Field | Meaning |\n",
        "|-------|---------|\n",
        "| **[ID](ca://s?q=Explain_the_dataset_ID_field)** | Record identifier. |\n",
        "| **[SiteID](ca://s?q=Describe_the_SiteID_monitoring_station_field)** | Monitoring station identifier. |\n",
        "| **[ObservationTimeUTC](ca://s?q=Explain_ObservationTimeUTC_timestamp_format)** | Timestamp for the start of the hourly measurement period. |\n",
        "| **[Value](ca://s?q=Explain_the_PM2.5_Value_field)** | PM₂.₅ concentration in micrograms per cubic meter. |\n",
        "\n",
        "### **Data Citation**:\n",
        "New York City Department of Health and Mental Hygiene and Queens College. New York City Community Air Survey. Real-time PM2.5 Monitor Data from 05-01-2026 to 05-19-2026. https://a816-dohbesp.nyc.gov/IndicatorPublic/data-features/realtime-air-quality/.\n",
        "\n",
        "Date downloaded: 05/19/26.\n",
        "\n",
        "Note: Data are preliminary and subject to change. External factors can sometimes affect monitor functioning and make data temporarily unavailable."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "r_tEnNnsTf77"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# **1. Load Libraries**"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "Cxo010jaMfmH"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "ZXfXdDgm29w6"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "import seaborn as sns\n",
        "\n",
        "# EDA display settings: show all DataFrame columns and control console output width in Colab\n",
        "pd.set_option(\"display.max_columns\", None)\n",
        "pd.set_option(\"display.width\", 120)\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# **2. Load Source Data**"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "XHJe7xGiT51k"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The Capstone reference file had timestamp formatting issues after CSV export, so the original clean PM2.5 file will used as the timestamp-safe source of truth. The Capstone reference file will used only to identify which PM2.5 `Value` records were intentionally set to missing for imputation practice.\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "b_L8Q9micS1-"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# ============================================================\n",
        "# Capstone Project: EDA for PM2.5 in NYC, May 2026\n",
        "# Data Loading Strategy:\n",
        "# 1. Load original clean dataset as timestamp-safe source of truth.\n",
        "# 2. Load capstone dataset only to identify missing Value cells.\n",
        "# 3. Transfer missing-value pattern by ID.\n",
        "# 4. Impute missing values.\n",
        "# 5. Perform EDA.\n",
        "# ============================================================\n",
        "\n",
        "SOURCE_PM25_URL = \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Hanner-1/pm25-nyc-capstone-eda/refs/heads/main/PM2.5_may_2026.csv\"\n",
        "CAPSTONE_PM25_URL = \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Hanner-1/pm25-nyc-capstone-eda/refs/heads/main/PM2.5_may_2026_Capstone.csv\"\n",
        "SITE_INFO_URL = \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Hanner-1/pm25-nyc-capstone-eda/refs/heads/main/site_info.csv\"\n",
        "\n",
        "source_df = pd.read_csv(SOURCE_PM25_URL)\n",
        "capstone_missing_ref_df = pd.read_csv(CAPSTONE_PM25_URL)\n",
        "site_info_df = pd.read_csv(SITE_INFO_URL)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Source PM2.5 data loaded:\", source_df.shape)\n",
        "print(\"Capstone missing-reference data loaded:\", capstone_missing_ref_df.shape)\n",
        "print(\"Site info data loaded:\", site_info_df.shape)\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "j4SbyO_NT7_3",
        "outputId": "24063689-072a-4267-ef86-4def93c33cdf"
      },
